-- title:
--   Horizontal primes of a crossing stalk as kernels of sections
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a level $M \ne 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that maps to $1$ under $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$, with $M/p \ne 0$, and assume the $q$-expansion $j$ lies in the function field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` (properness, flatness, integrality and local finite presentation of `toBase` at level $\Gamma_M(M,H)$, normality on affine opens, a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` and an isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ onto the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, together with further compatibilities). Let $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ be a valuation subring with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ a ring map inducing the structural map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by $p$, together with $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa(A)$, $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $\iota_A : O \to A$ compatible with $\rho$, with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and with the residue map of $A$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,h_A\,\rho\,h_\rho\,0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,A\,h_A\,\rho\,h_\rho\,1$ into the fibre of the model over $\kappa(A)$, and $U$ an open of $X_O = \mathfrak{X} \times_{R_p} \operatorname{Spec} O$ containing the image of $n$ under $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ followed by the first comparison morphism followed by the base-change map `bcMap`. Let $O'$ be a further discrete valuation ring with uniformiser $\varpi'$, $\sigma : O \to O'$, and $\iota_{A'} : O' \to A$ injective and local with $\iota_{A'} \circ \sigma = \iota_A$, plus $j_{O'} : O' \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and the corresponding compatibilities over $R_p$. Write $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ for the base change of the model to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, $\mathrm{prJ}$ and $\mathrm{prJ}'$ for the maps $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_O$, $X_{O'}$ induced by $j_O$, $j_{O'}$, $x_n'$ for the image of $n$ in $X_{O'} = \mathfrak{X} \times_{R_p} \operatorname{Spec} O'$, $B$ for the stalk of $X_{O'}$ at $x_n'$, and $\sigma_B : O' \to B$ for the map on constants obtained from the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O'$ and the germ at $x_n'$. The assertion is: for every prime ideal $P$ of $B$ with $P \ne \bot$ and $\sigma_B(\varpi') \notin P$, there are a place $W$ of `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (that is, `W.IsRational`) and a morphism $s : \operatorname{Spec} A \to U$ such that $s$ followed by $U \hookrightarrow X_O$ and the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ is $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_A)$, the restriction of $s$ along $\operatorname{Spec} \overline{\mathbb{Q}} \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ corresponding to $W$ under `pointEquivPlace` followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and $\mathrm{prJ}$, and $s$ sends the closed point of $A$ to the image of $n$ in $X_O$; and, moreover, for every $s' : \operatorname{Spec} A \to X_{O'}$ agreeing with $s$ after projection to the model, lying over $\operatorname{Spec}(\iota_{A'})$, and sending the closed point of $A$ to $x_n'$, the local ring map $\chi : B \to A$ obtained from `Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo s'` and the specialisation map of stalks satisfies $b \in P \iff \chi(b) = 0$ for all $b \in B$, i.e. $P = \ker \chi$.
--
--   This is the statement that every prime of the local ring at a crossing point of the Deligne–Rapoport model which is non-zero and horizontal (does not contain the uniformiser of the base) is the centre of a rational place of the function field, realised as the kernel of the map on stalks induced by an $A$-valued section through the crossing. It is used in the analysis of the crossing (node) ring of $X_H(M)$ at $p$, feeding the two results on unit readings and vanishing orders at crossings and on the identification of the completed local ring with that of the standard crossing model.
